# Infinities and NaNs must pass msil-verify. The backend loads them with
# 'ldc.r4 float32(0x...)' and 'ldc.r8 float64(0x...)'; the .NET Framework 4.8
# ildasm prints several back as 'inf', '-inf', 'nan', '-nan', '-nan(ind)',
# 'nan(snan)' or '-nan(snan)', which ilasm cannot parse, so the neutralized
# pass of msil-verify.py (pass 2, which needs ildasm) could not reassemble its
# copy of a valid module. Inputs/fp-special-constants.il has one method per
# constant (its header lists what ildasm prints for each): +inf and -inf of
# both widths, -nan(ind) of both widths, float64 signaling NaNs of both
# signs, float32 signaling NaNs (ilasm quiets them) and payload NaNs, some of
# which ildasm prints as bytes that reassemble as they are. The modern ildasm
# prints all of them as bytes. The module also force-JITs and runs: exit 42.
# REQUIRES: msil-ilverify, msil-ildasm

# RUN: %ilasm -dll -output=%t.dll %S/Inputs/fp-special-constants.il
# RUN: %msil_verify %t.dll
# RUN: %if msil-jitall %{ %msil_jitall %t.dll %}
# RUN: %msil_exec --out %t.out %t.dll
# RUN: %{harness_check} equals %t.out "[exit 42]"
